            <div xml:id="d663">

                <pb facs="0787" n="685" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 3742/36–42.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Coombs to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-09-28"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">September 28, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 170.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to state that Mr. Leguia
                    was inaugurated President of Peru on the 24th instant with the usual ceremony
                    for conducting the transmission of power from the outgoing to the incoming
                    President.</p>
                <p>The ceremony, which took place in the new House of Deputies, was dignified and
                    impressive.</p>
                <p>The diplomatic and consular corps were present by invitation.</p>
                <p>On the next day, the 25th, the new President, attended by his cabinet, received
                    the diplomatic corps at the palace, and afterwards I called upon the retiring
                    President, Mr. Pardo.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Leslie Coombs.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
